From e90a69172f4c74eabc4e0dd295314f28697b1333 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: its screens in place of the launcher, its settings in
 games

Built with PW_PC5 (PC5, PPSA11018) the title shows PC5's screens
(native/pc5_*.c, added by the PC5 build) instead of the launcher;
choosing a game reads the profiles again, so a game PC5 just installed
starts, and restarts the title into it. If PC5's files are missing from
the app, or it can't open the screen, the launcher is shown as before.

In a game, with PW_PC5:
- Wine gets LC_ALL from the PS5's language (Wine takes the Windows
  language from it when setlocale has nothing), and RADV's shader cache
  is kept in the game's own prefix (pc5-cache/radv);
- PC5's loading screen replaces the spinner until the first picture;
- the touchpad and Options held for two seconds close the game (Alt+F4,
  ended after five seconds as before), with a short buzz;
- PC5's settings apply (pc5_game.h): the game's rumble or none, the
  light bar in the game's colour or the screen's, the triggers' rumble
  or resistance, and the frame counter in a corner.

libvulkan.prx (wine/ps5/pw_vulkan_radv.c, tools/link_radv_prx.sh): RADV's
framebuffer registrations and flips are wrapped too. Each flip counts
towards the frame counter, which VideoOut's second hardware cursor shows
(pw_pc5_hud, drawn from the title's loop by pw_pc5_hud_tick: RADV flips
with its output's lock held); the shown framebuffer's colour is read for
the light bar (pw_pc5_screen_color: texels spread over it, whose tiling
only reorders them). wine/ps5/pw_pc5_hud.h draws the counter for both.

For any build: the library holds 128 games (PW_WINE_LIBRARY_MAX,
PW_PROFILE_CATALOG_MAX); PW_TITLE_ID and PW_WINE64_ROOT_DATA can be set;
the sandbox instance holding the runtime is looked for once /data is
granted (the console counts _000, _001, ... up when one is left behind),
for the runtime and for restarting the title; and
tools/build_native.sh takes PW_TITLE_ID, PW_LAPY_DIR (a Lapy helper built
for that title), PW_EXTRA_SOURCES, PW_EXTRA_CFLAGS and PW_EXTRA_LIBS.

